#BlueJ class context
comment0.target=Simulator
comment0.text=\n\ A\ more\ advanced\ predator-prey\ simulator,\ based\ on\ a\ rectangular\ field\ containing\n\ a\ variety\ of\ animals.\n\n\ @author\ David\ J.\ Barnes\n\ @author\ Michael\ K\u00F6lling\n\ @author\ Karim\ Malik\n\ @author\ Ayan\ Mamun\n\ @version\ 7.2\n
comment1.params=
comment1.target=Simulator()
comment1.text=\n\ Construct\ a\ simulation\ field\ with\ default\ size.\n
comment2.params=depth\ width
comment2.target=Simulator(int,\ int)
comment2.text=\n\ Create\ a\ simulation\ field\ with\ the\ given\ size.\n\n\ @param\ depth\ Depth\ of\ the\ field.\ Must\ be\ greater\ than\ zero.\n\ @param\ width\ Width\ of\ the\ field.\ Must\ be\ greater\ than\ zero.\n
comment3.params=numSteps
comment3.target=void\ simulate(int)
comment3.text=\n\ Run\ the\ simulation\ for\ the\ given\ number\ of\ steps.\n\n\ @param\ numSteps\ The\ number\ of\ steps\ to\ run\ for.\n
comment4.params=
comment4.target=void\ simulateOneStep()
comment4.text=\n\ Run\ the\ simulation\ from\ its\ current\ stage\ for\ a\ single\ step,\ update\ its\ clock\ and\ weather\ conditions,\n\ and\ iterate\ over\ the\ whole\ field\ updating\ the\ state\ of\ entity.\n
comment5.params=
comment5.target=void\ reset()
comment5.text=\n\ Reset\ the\ simulation\ to\ a\ starting\ position.\n
comment6.params=
comment6.target=void\ populate()
comment6.text=\n\ Randomly\ populate\ the\ current\ field\ using\ the\ {@link\ Simulator\#populationSpawner}.\n
comment7.params=
comment7.target=void\ reportStats()
comment7.text=\n\ Report\ on\ the\ number\ of\ each\ type\ of\ animal\ in\ the\ field.\n
comment8.params=milliseconds
comment8.target=void\ delay(int)
comment8.text=\n\ Pause\ for\ a\ given\ time.\n\n\ @param\ milliseconds\ The\ time\ to\ pause\ for,\ in\ milliseconds\n
